---
// The hamsa, the open hand that turns the evil eye away, hung fingers down
// from a peg as the charm is hung. It is line alone, with no ground of its
// own, so the page shows through it: three round fingers between two pointed
// side fingers, one lidded eye in the palm under a lotus, scallops overlapping
// around it, and eye beads and drops on chains below. It swings from the peg
// as a pendulum, and the pendants swing from it. It heads the closing section
// of the homepage.
---

<!-- The view box is wider than the hand by 40 a side: that is the room the swing and the side pendants need. -->
<svg viewBox="-40 0 480 650" class="block w-full h-full overflow-visible" aria-hidden="true">
